  "enisaUuid": "a8e9f48f-a630-3343-8de5-715de11faa44",
  "description": "In RealVNC Server before 7.19.1, UDP-based connections could potentially be exploited without authentication to execute code remotely or cause the software to crash. This could allow an attacker to remotely execute code as root on certain platforms or perform a denial of service attack. This issue affects RealVNC Viewer: from 8.4.0 through 8.6.1; RealVNC Classic Viewer: from 6.4.0 through 7.18.2; RealVNC Server: from 6.4.0 through 7.19.0; RealVNC Connect App: through 8.6.1; RealVNC iOS Viewer: from 3.7.0 through 4.9.5; RealVNC Android Viewer: from 3.5.0 through 4.9.5; RealVNC iOS Server: through 2.8.1; RealVNC Android Server: through 2.8.3; On-Demand Assist: through 3.4.1.",
  "datePublished": "Nov 27, 2026, 5:52:17 AM",
